note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
note Test-only entry appended after om/disasm/sm121_dis.om by mk/om-disasm.mk: no sm_121 row prints a float
note immediate today, so the differential reaches fimm through this entry and compares it with the C's fimm
note (printf %.*g, the shortest precision that sscanf reads back) over the binary32 sweep.
note u is the float's bits; the result is the text length.
fn fimm_probe u view ulong 1 o edit uchar ON to ulong
note omega-bridge bc11b30b takes only a literal new length: 1024 is PW
pl = new ulong 1024 0
pinit pl
ret fimm o 0 pl get u 0
end
